0008-xlsx-visibility-keeps-calc: row/column visibility and size ops keep
formula results instead of forcing a full recalculation.

- betteroffice-xlsx CalculationScope: SetRow/ColVisibility, SetRowHeight,
  SetColWidth and RestoreRow/ColDimension (the undo path of visibility and
  size ops) map to Kept. xlsx-calc reads neither visibility nor sizes:
  SUBTOTAL 101-111 behaves like 1-11 and AGGREGATE ignores its
  ignore-hidden options (xlsx-calc functions/stats.rs `subtotal`,
  `aggregate`). A full recalc on these ops never changed a value; on the
  Dalia databook it cost ~4.3 s per outline toggle.
- Test: visibility_keeps_formula_results (SUBTOTAL(109) + SUM, row and col
  hide/show, undo): values, calculation counters and evaluated formulas
  unchanged.
- All 6 dimension ops are Kept: xlsx-calc reads neither visibility nor
  row heights / column widths (no CELL("width"), no INFO; OFFSET height/
  width are arguments, not geometry). Checked by grep over xlsx-calc/src.

KNOWN GAP
SUBTOTAL 101-111 and AGGREGATE do not skip hidden rows (upstream, not this
patch). If hidden rows ever get modelled, restore a scoped recalculation of
hidden-aware formulas and their dependents on these ops.

